    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0857" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/388: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-04T17:00:00+01:00">October 4, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 4—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>282. From Reber. My telegram No. 276,
                    October 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>], p.m.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d566-f1"
                    /> The President of the Liberian Committee informs me that the Liberian
                    representatives have “accepted the plan on behalf of their Government subject to
                    a successful outcome of negotiations with the American group interested.”<anchor
                        n="75" xml:id="d566-f2"/></p>
                <p>Inasmuch as a modification of the Finance Corporation’s contract will be required
                    to make effective this scheme and provide the funds for its execution this last
                    clause was considered essential.</p>
                <p>With this understanding the Government of Liberia has accepted the plan of
                    assistance as adopted by the Committee.</p>
                <p>In his telegram of reply the President likewise has asked me to inform him as
                    soon as possible when the Finance Corporation representatives could be expected
                    to commence the negotiations. [Reber.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
